<title>SUDAN: Chinese company awarded gold concession in Sudan.</title>
<headline>Chinese company awarded gold concession in Sudan.</headline>
<dateline>KHARTOUM 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sudan has awarded the Chinese company Dong Ling a concession to prospect for gold in northeast Sudan, the official news agency SUNA said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The agreement was signed in Khartoum on Wednesday by Energy and Mining Minister Awad Ahmad al-Jaz and Wang Kin, chairwoman of the Chinese company.</p>
<p>The agency said mining in the Sholai area of the Red Sea state was expected to start next year. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Ariab, a Sudanese-French joint venture, has been mining gold in the Red Sea hills area since 1991.</p>
</text>
